md`# brain-secrets

The secrets a Cloud Brain holds for its Workers. The methods are \`brain-db\`'s, and their rules at the core are fixed.

| | |
|---|---|
| \`secret.list\` | query, owner. \`{ secrets: [{ name, setAt, rule }] }\`. No values. A copy also has \`copiedFrom\` and \`by\`. |
| \`secret.put\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ name, value }\`. A name is capitals, digits and \`_\`, and does not start with \`BRAIN_\` or \`CF_\`. |
| \`secret.get\` | query. \`?name=\`. The owner's own session; or a Worker, for a secret whose rule allows it. |
| \`secret.delete\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ name }\`. Its rule goes with it. |
| \`secret.setRule\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ name, allow }\`: an expression over \`caller\` and \`resource { name, op }\`. \`allow: null\` removes it. |
| \`secret.copy\` | procedure. \`{ from, to }\` answers \`{ from, to, setAt, rule }\`. The owner's own session, or a turn the owner sent that only the owner reads. Added 2026-10-07. |

A Worker reads a secret while it runs: \`await secrets.NAME\` asks \`secret.get\` as that Worker and holds the answer for 5 s, so a new value or a changed rule is followed within that and nothing is deployed. A secret with no rule is read by no Worker. A token, a granted account and an anonymous caller are refused \`secret.get\` whatever a rule says, and only the owner's own session writes.

\`secret.copy\` gives a value a second name inside \`brain-db\`. The value is in no answer, so a service can change the name of a secret it reads and no page or model holds the value. \`to\` must not be set and obeys the name rule of \`secret.put\`. The rule of \`from\` goes to \`to\` unchanged; a rule that reads \`resource\` is refused, because it would decide differently under the new name. \`from\` stays. A turn copies 10 secrets a day. A token, a granted account, the owner through a PDS, a member and a Worker are refused. This page has no control for it.

It does not reach the key that signs sessions (\`SESSION_KEY\`, before 2026-10-07 \`COOKIE_KEY\`). The deployer binds that key to the kernel at deploy, and it is not in this store.

**Set secret** on a secret with no rule gives it one that names the Workers whose services name the secret:

\`\`\`js
caller.worker in ["brain-x-whatsapp"]
\`\`\`

The kernel's cookie key and each Worker's own key are not here. The deployer binds those at deploy.`
// %%
// The Workers and the secrets each names come from the Brain, so this module needs none of the Brain's own modules.
secretsView = secretsPanel({
  client: brainClient,
  signedIn: !!brainWho.owner,
  services: brainWho.owner ? (await brainClient.query("service.list").catch(() => ({ services: [] }))).services : []
})
// %%
secretsPanel = ({ client, signedIn = false, services = [] } = {}) => {
  const muted = "color:var(--theme-foreground-muted)";
  if (!client || !signedIn) return htl.html`<i style=${muted}>Sign in as the owner to see secrets.</i>`;
  const out = htl.html`<div></div>`, note = htl.html`<span style=${muted}></span>`;
  const name = Inputs.text({ placeholder: "NAME", width: 200 });
  const value = Inputs.password({ placeholder: "value", width: 220 });
  const rule = Inputs.text({ placeholder: "rule; empty: the Workers that name it", width: 320 });
  const users = (n) => services.filter((r) => (r.secrets || []).includes(n)).map((r) => r.worker);
  let listed = [];
  const draw = async () => {
    listed = (await client.query("secret.list")).secrets;
    const wanted = [...new Set(services.flatMap((r) => r.secrets || []))].filter((n) => !/^(BRAIN_|CF_|COOKIE_KEY$|SESSION_KEY$|RECOVERY_KEY$)/.test(n) && !listed.some((s) => s.name === n));
    const data = [
      ...listed.map((s) => ({ name: s.name, state: "set", "named by": users(s.name).join(", "), "read by": s.rule || "no Worker", set: new Date(s.setAt) })),
      ...wanted.map((n) => ({ name: n, state: "not set", "named by": users(n).join(", "), "read by": "", set: null }))
    ];
    out.replaceChildren(data.length ? Inputs.table(data, { select: false, layout: "auto", format: { set: (d) => (d ? d.toISOString().slice(0, 10) : "") } }) : htl.html`<i style=${muted}>No secrets.</i>`);
  };
  const act = (label, fn) =>
    Inputs.button(label, {
      reduce: async () => {
        try {
          note.textContent = await fn(name.value.trim());
          await draw();
        } catch (e) {
          note.textContent = "Not done: " + e.message;
        }
      }
    });
  // Workers read a secret while they run, so a new value needs no deploy. A secret with no rule is given one that
  // names the Workers whose services name the secret.
  const set = act("Set secret", async (n) => {
    await client.procedure("secret.put", { name: n, value: value.value });
    value.value = "";
    const typed = rule.value.trim(), has = listed.find((s) => s.name === n)?.rule;
    const allow = typed || (!has && users(n).length ? `caller.worker in ${JSON.stringify(users(n))}` : "");
    if (allow) await client.procedure("secret.setRule", { name: n, allow });
    return `${n} is set.${allow ? " Read by: " + allow : has ? "" : " No Worker reads it until it has a rule."}`;
  });
  const setRule = act("Set rule", async (n) => {
    const done = await client.procedure("secret.setRule", { name: n, allow: rule.value.trim() || null });
    return done.allow === null ? `${n}: no Worker reads it.` : `${n} is read by: ${done.allow}`;
  });
  draw().catch((e) => (note.textContent = "secret.list failed: " + e.message));
  return htl.html`<div>${out}<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;margin-top:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center">${name}${value}${rule}${set}${setRule}</div><div style="margin-top:6px">${note}</div></div>`;
}
// %%
md`## Tests`
// %%
test_secrets_panel_lists_set_and_missing = {
  const calls = [];
  const client = {
    query: async (m) => (calls.push(m), { secrets: [{ name: "WA_TOKEN", setAt: Date.UTC(2026, 9, 6), rule: null }] }),
    procedure: async (m, input) => (calls.push([m, input.name, input.allow]), { allow: input.allow })
  };
  const el = secretsPanel({ client, signedIn: true, services: [{ worker: "brain-x-whatsapp", secrets: ["WA_TOKEN", "WA_VERIFY", "BRAIN_KEY"] }] });
  for (let i = 0; i < 50 && !el.querySelector("table"); i++) await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 20));
  const text = el.querySelector("table").textContent;
  expect(calls).toEqual(["secret.list"]);
  expect(/WA_TOKEN/.test(text) && /WA_VERIFY/.test(text) && /not set/.test(text)).toBe(true);
  // A name the platform sets is not asked for.
  expect(/BRAIN_KEY/.test(text)).toBe(false);
  expect(secretsPanel({ client: null }).textContent).toBe("Sign in as the owner to see secrets.");
  // Setting a secret with no rule gives it one naming the Workers whose services name it. Nothing is deployed.
  const [n, v] = el.querySelectorAll("input");
  n.value = "WA_VERIFY";
  v.value = "x";
  for (const i of [n, v]) i.dispatchEvent(new Event("input", { bubbles: true }));
  [...el.querySelectorAll("button")].find((b) => b.textContent === "Set secret").click();
  for (let i = 0; i < 50 && calls.length < 4; i++) await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 20));
  expect(calls.slice(1, 3)).toEqual([["secret.put", "WA_VERIFY", undefined], ["secret.setRule", "WA_VERIFY", 'caller.worker in ["brain-x-whatsapp"]']]);
  return "1 set, 1 missing, 1 given its default rule";
}
// %%
import {brainClient, brainWho} from "@tomlarkworthy/brain-shell"
// %%
import {expect} from "@tomlarkworthy/jest-expect-standalone"
